  "note": [
    "Scripture is Kulish (1905), the library's uk Bible, from the ebible mirror (bibles/ukr_pan, USFM), pasted by script. Spurgeon quotes almost entirely without citations, so every quotation was identified and looked up in the whole Bible on disk. A row is `mined` only when the translator reported it verbatim AND the block holds at least 45 characters (or the whole verse) of Kulish's wording, quote marks aside; short fragments, joined spans and re-personed quotations are self_rendered.",
    "Where Kulish's sense differs from the KJV point Spurgeon makes, Kulish is kept in the quote and Spurgeon's own sentences carry the point: Isaiah 45:22 «Обернїтесь» (turn) for 'Look'; Romans 5:6 «недужими» (weak) for 'without strength'; Isaiah 19:20 «спаса й оборонника» for 'a Saviour, and a great one'; Hebrews 9:12 «відкупленнє». Romans 4:5, the book's key text, is quoted as Kulish's participle «Оправдуючого нечестивого»; unquoted refrains are modern prose «Бог виправдовує нечестивого».",
    "AI-translated (job #5175) by fan-out over 9 translators against one pinned brief (titles, reader addressed as «ви», house book names, « » outer / „ “ nested); tag sequence identical to the English per chapter; awaiting native review."
  ],
